Methodology and How to Read the Report
Report organization: Overall is presented first as one complete scope chapter. Each approved site then receives its own complete chapter containing Executive Summary, selected-grain performance, supporting evidence, and taxonomy analysis.
Grain mode: Daily, Weekly, and Monthly are each analyzed independently and then synthesized in the executive summary.
Smiley Rate is weighted as SUM positive responses divided by SUM responses. The approved Smiley target is 81.50%.
Daily compares with the previous equivalent day. Weekly always uses a Sunday-through-Saturday calendar boundary. Current WTD compares with the same elapsed days in the preceding week.
Monthly uses the resolved reporting month. Current MTD compares with the same elapsed calendar days in the preceding month; a completed month compares with the complete preceding month.
Improving and Regressing are directional performance labels. Smiley Rate and QA Pass Rate improve when they increase; Unhappy Rate and QA Failure Rate improve when they decrease. Small movements within the configured threshold are Stable.
Volume movement is descriptive rather than positive or negative. The report labels volume as increased, decreased, or stable.
Executive trend images use Smiley Registered At as their date/time source and Smiley Rate is calculated as SUM positive responses divided by SUM responses.
All Rated includes Finance, Other, and Untagged/misc rated rows. Finance and Other remain separate comparison populations in the full report.
QA values use 1 = pass, 0 = fail, and blank = unavailable/not audited. Blank QA values are excluded from pass-rate denominators.
Ticket IDs are retained for auditability. PII is redacted only inside Smiley Comment before published outputs are created.
Overall executive metrics include all sites that pass the selected LOB/business filters. Named site chapters are limited to the approved CORE list: ARN, HTW, MTQ, PHX.
Finance tickets are identified when either Level One or Level Two matches the configured Finance taxonomy. Blank, misc, and untagged topic rows remain separate from Other.
Smiley is the positive outcome. Smiley Rate equals Smiley divided by Rated. Neutral and Frownie counts remain visible as operational driver indicators.
QA values use valid audited values only: 1 = pass, 0 = fail, and blank/invalid values are excluded from the denominator.
Finance Audited and Other Audited are the valid QA sample sizes. Finance Gap pp equals Finance Pass Rate minus Other Pass Rate.
Finance Neutral Fail and Finance Frownie Fail show the QA failure rate within those Finance rating groups. Their audited counts are shown beside the rates so 0.0% is not mistaken for a large sample.
The QA tables show association, not proof that a failed attribute caused a Neutral or Frownie rating. They should be combined with ticket review and operational context.
Squads with fewer than 30 rated Finance responses are Small sample. Squads below 40 are Directional. Better or Worse requires the comparison threshold, a practical gap of at least 3.0 pp, and a two-sided statistical check versus the remaining Finance population.
Created Date is interpreted in UTC and is not converted to Manila time. The full timestamp is preserved for hour/day analysis while a separate normalized UTC date supports period filtering.
Monthly trend compares All Rated, Finance, and Other using Smiley Rate. Time-of-day, day-of-week, and day-of-month sections compare matching segments with the previous equivalent reporting window.
Smiley Rate and QA Pass Rate improve when they increase. An absolute movement below 0.5 percentage points is Stable.
Volume is descriptive rather than good or bad. An absolute change below 5.0% is Stable volume; otherwise the report states Volume increased or Volume decreased.

